    "m2_prompt_trader_proposal_original": "**Action**: Hold\n\n**Reasoning**: The evidence is genuinely balanced and supports maintaining the current position rather than committing new capital. The bull case rests on solid long-term technicals \u2014 price at $184.30 sits 16.6% above a rising 200-day SMA ($158.05), the 50-day SMA has been reclaimed, MACD histogram just flipped positive, and RSI recovered from oversold (36.75) to neutral (54.78). However, the bear's core technical concern is legitimate: the bounce is occurring on 23% BELOW-average volume (relative volume 0.77), which undermines the institutional-accumulation thesis, and the stock remains below the $188.77\u2013$189.50 resistance zone that rejected it once already. With negative 20-day momentum (-2.74%), MACD still in negative territory (-0.22), and the stock hugging support just ~$1.77 above the 50-day SMA, there is no confirmation of a breakout. The prudent action is to hold and wait for either a confirmed breakout above $189.50 on above-average volume (relative volume > 1.2) or a pullback to the $176\u2013177 support zone for a better entry, with a risk-management exit if price breaks below $176.44 toward the 200-day SMA at $158.05.\n\n**Entry Price**: 184.3\n\n**Stop Loss**: 176.44\n\n**Position Sizing**: Maintain moderate weight (roughly benchmark or slightly below) until one of the two trigger conditions is met \u2014 a confirmed breakout above $189.50 on above-average volume, or a pullback to the $176\u2013177 support zone.\n\nFINAL TRANSACTION PROPOSAL: **HOLD**",
